# Webkitten

Webkitten is a Java desktop browser project built on JavaFX WebView, which provides a WebKit-backed browsing surface for desktop applications.

## Included features

- Multi-tab browsing
- Address bar navigation
- Back, forward, reload, home controls
- Bookmarks and quick bookmark menu
- Browsing history panel
- Simple download manager that saves pages to a local downloads folder
- Custom browser chrome and toolbar
- Embedded dev tools panel for status and alert output
- JavaFX-based desktop shell

## Tech stack

- Java 17+
- Maven
- JavaFX 21
- WebView / WebKit backend

## Run the app

```bash
mvn clean javafx:run
```

## Project layout

- `pom.xml` — Maven configuration
- `src/main/java/com/webkitten/browser/Main.java` — browser UI and application logic

## Notes

This project uses JavaFX's `WebView`, which delegates to the operating system's WebKit implementation. That makes it the best Java option for a browser shell without replacing the browser engine with a custom rendering layer.

If you want a more advanced browser in a future step, the next additions could include:

- tab drag-and-drop
- secure certificate handling
- a real DOM inspector
- cookie management
- custom search engine integration
- a full menu-based browser shell

## Browser architecture

The UI is intentionally organized around a modern tabbed desktop browser design:

- toolbar with navigation and address controls
- tab pane for multiple pages
- right-side sidebar for bookmarks, history, and downloads
- bottom dev tools panel for debugging state and page events

This gives the project a good base for expanding into a heavier browser product later.


